The diagnostic will test four falsifiable explanations in order:

1. Information loss: if even a flexible held-out model on the 16 slots stays near the floors, the ceiling is informational.
2. Sealed-head capacity: if wider ReLU heads materially beat `(8,)` while the flexible model is strong, the bottleneck is architectural.
3. Cross-world shift: if leave-one-anchor-out is useful but leave-one-world-out collapses, the information is locally learnable but not portable.
4. Target difficulty rather than training mechanics: if the same sealed training code performs well on the shipped surrogate and poorly on the declared target, the contrast is target-specific.

The tight checkable criterion is a validator over `results.json` that fails unless both worlds are present, at least 60 exact-path anchors are measured, gauge and decomposition residuals are reported, every required model has both holdout regimes and all three metrics, and all 16 permutation importances are present.
