codex
The measured first anchors are 434 s (world 1) and 406 s (world 2), with 992/987 rows. Both have exact `0.0` base gauge; the stored-vs-recomputed decomposition residual is `8.88e-16`, and the independent `c1_difference_surplus` residual is below `2.3e-14`. This confirms the slower density regime. I’m checking whether later anchors benefit from warm caches before repartitioning the remaining work.
